        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Henry's driveway range is simpler than the shelf makes it look: four asphalt emulsions ranked by solids and warranty, and three repair products that matter as much as the sealer. The 200 E-Z Stir is the sensible default and the 532 is for rough asphalt. In both cases the warranty is a defect promise, not a schedule.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Repair the cracks, wait for a 48-hour dry and warm window, put down one well-worked coat, and keep cars off until it has properly set. That routine does more for how long a Henry sealcoat lasts than which of the four pails you choose.
          </p>
